# ERROR RESILIENCE PROTOCOL: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2.15

> "Assume the network will fail, the database will timeout, and the user will click twice."

## 1. NEXT.JS APP ROUTER BOUNDARIES (`error.tsx`)
Every Route Group or core segment MUST have an `error.tsx` file.
```tsx
'use client';

import * as Sentry from '@sentry/nextjs';
import { useEffect } from 'react';

export default function ErrorBoundary({ error, reset }: { error: Error & { digest?: string }; reset: () => void }) {
  useEffect(() => {
    // 1. Log to Sentry immediately
    Sentry.captureException(error);
    // 2. Log strictly to console for developers
    console.error('Segment Error Caught:', error);
  }, [error]);

  return (
    <div className="flex flex-col items-center justify-center p-8 text-center bg-red-500/10 rounded-xl border border-red-500/20">
      <h2 className="text-xl font-bold text-red-100 mb-2">System Interruption</h2>
      <p className="text-red-200/70 mb-6 text-sm">We've logged the issue and are investigating.</p>
      <button 
        onClick={() => reset()} 
        className="px-4 py-2 bg-red-600 hover:bg-red-500 text-white rounded-md transition-colors"
      >
        Attempt Recovery
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## 2. ASYNC OPERATION SAFETY
Do NOT let unhandled promise rejections crash the thread. Wrap all external calls:
```typescript
import { toast } from 'sonner';

export async function safeExecute(action: () => Promise<void>, errorMessage = "Action failed") {
  try {
    await action();
  } catch (error) {
    Sentry.captureException(error);
    console.error(`[EXECUTION_FAILED] ${errorMessage}`, error);
    toast.error(errorMessage);
    throw error; // Re-throw only if upstream logic needs to halt
  }
}
```

## 3. ZOD EVERYTHING
Never trust external payload shapes. Validate at the boundaries.
```typescript
const UserSchema = z.object({ id: z.string(), email: z.string().email() });

// ❌ BANNED: Trusting the boundary
const data = await res.json();
setUser(data);

// ✅ REQUIRED: Validating the boundary
const result = UserSchema.safeParse(await res.json());
if (!result.success) {
  Sentry.captureException(result.error);
  toast.error("Invalid data received");
  return;
}
setUser(result.data);
```

## 4. CONSOLE HYGIENE
- Treat console *warnings* (`console.warn`) as errors in development. Fix React keys, missing dependencies, or unmounted state updates instantly.
- Do not deploy with generic `console.log("here")` markers. Use structured `{ logger }` from `firebase-functions` on the backend.
